  partId: pressure_vessel
  displayName: Crew Module Pressure Vessel
  shortName: Pressure Vessel
  zone: 1
  order: 90
  keySpec: "8.95 m\xB3 habitable  \xB7  Al-Li 2219"
  summary: "The sealed aluminium-lithium structure the crew live inside. It is machined
    and friction-stir-welded from seven large pieces.\n\nTotal pressurised volume
    is 19.56 m\xB3, of which 8.95 m\xB3 is habitable \u2014 about the space of two
    large telephone boxes, for four people for up to 21 days."
  whyItMatters: Friction stir welding stirs the two pieces together while still solid,
    so the metal never melts. Fewer weld defects means less structural margin has
    to be carried for uncertainty, which means less mass.
  narration: {fileID: 0}
